<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_commands",
    "Set the server's Message of the Day — a welcome message shown to all users when they connect."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_question}>{dgettext("help_commands", "When to Use It")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_commands",
    "Use it to greet people, point them to the server rules, or share news that everyone should see when they connect."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_code}>{dgettext("help_commands", "Syntax")}</.help_h4>
<pre>{dgettext("help_commands", "/setmotd <text>")}</pre>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_tag}>{dgettext("help_commands", "Parameters")}</.help_h4>
<p><code>text</code> {dgettext("help_commands", "— The MOTD content to display.")}</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_tab_control}>{dgettext("help_commands", "How It Works")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_commands",
    "Sets or replaces the server MOTD. After setting it, all newly connecting users will see this message in the Status tab when they join. Any previous MOTD is replaced."
  )}
</p>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_commands",
    "Users who are already connected get a short note in their Status window that the MOTD changed. They can read the new text with %{command}.",
    command: "/motd"
  )}
</p>
<p>
  {dgettext(
    "help_commands",
    "Everything you type after the command becomes the MOTD, with your spacing kept. The text is saved in the server settings, so it stays after a server restart. You get a confirmation line when it is saved. Administrators can also edit the MOTD in the Admin MOTD window of the Admin Console."
  )}
</p>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_rules}>{dgettext("help_commands", "Rules & Limits")}</.help_h4>
<ul>
  <li>{dgettext("help_commands", "Server administrator only")}</li>
  <li>{dgettext("help_commands", "Message text is required")}</li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_commands",
      "You must be identified with NickServ for your administrator role to count"
    )}
  </li>
  <li>{dgettext("help_commands", "Other users get a permission denied error")}</li>
  <li>
    {dgettext(
      "help_commands",
      "Without text, you see the usage line and the current MOTD is kept"
    )}
  </li>
</ul>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_lightbulb}>{dgettext("help_commands", "Examples")}</.help_h4>
<pre>{dgettext("help_commands", "/setmotd Welcome to RetroHexChat! Please read the rules in #rules.")}</pre>
<.help_h4 icon={:icon_link}>{dgettext("help_commands", "See Also")}</.help_h4>
<p>
  <.help_link topic="cmd-motd">{dgettext("help_commands", "/motd")}</.help_link>
  · <.help_link topic="cmd-clearmotd">{dgettext("help_commands", "/clearmotd")}</.help_link>
  · <.help_link topic="feature-admin-motd">{dgettext("help_commands", "Admin MOTD")}</.help_link>
  ·
  <.help_link topic="feature-special-messages">
    {dgettext("help_commands", "Special Messages")}
  </.help_link>
</p>
